        },
        {
          "id": "doc-67fcc48de84f::sentence-229",
          "documentId": "doc-67fcc48de84f",
          "text": "Kelly (MS) | Kelly (MS) | Republican | MS | Yea |\n",
          "start": 10083,
          "end": 10133,
          "context": "Kelly (IL) | Kelly (IL) | Democratic | IL | Nay |\n Kelly (MS) | Kelly (MS) | Republican | MS | Yea |\n Kelly (PA) | Kelly (PA) | Republican | PA | Yea |\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-67fcc48de84f::sentence-287",
          "documentId": "doc-67fcc48de84f",
          "text": "McEachin | McEachin | Democratic | VA | Nay |\n",
          "start": 12780,
          "end": 12826,
          "context": "McCollum | McCollum | Democratic | MN | Nay |\n McEachin | McEachin | Democratic | VA | Nay |\n McGovern | McGovern | Democratic | MA | Nay |\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-b7039c2b13f6::sentence-7",
          "documentId": "doc-b7039c2b13f6",
          "text": "I support reform such as modernizing the retirement age and indexing it to life expectancy. ",
          "start": 654,
          "end": 746,
          "context": "But no longer can we simply “protect” Social Security as some politicians seek to do; we must make needed reforms to “preserve” it for future generations.  I support reform such as modernizing the retirement age and indexing it to life expectancy.  I also support giving younger workers the opportunity to invest a portion of their money in optional personal accounts. "
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-b7039c2b13f6::sentence-2",
          "documentId": "doc-b7039c2b13f6",
          "text": "Is Social Security, as it now exists, survivable and would you support raising the cap on earning, raising the retirement age, reducing payments to wealthier Americans and allow younger workers to invest a portion of the Social Security into private accounts? ",
          "start": 11,
          "end": 271,
          "context": "Question 3\n Is Social Security, as it now exists, survivable and would you support raising the cap on earning, raising the retirement age, reducing payments to wealthier Americans and allow younger workers to invest a portion of the Social Security into private accounts?  What proposals would you make to ensure it is available for future generations?\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-b7039c2b13f6::sentence-33",
          "documentId": "doc-b7039c2b13f6",
          "text": "America must honor the promises made to those receiving benefits or about to receive benefits. ",
          "start": 3664,
          "end": 3759,
          "context": "That has contributed in part to the challenges we face.  America must honor the promises made to those receiving benefits or about to receive benefits.  For future workers, alterations will be needed to when benefits can commence. "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "atomId": "atom-2",
      "spans": [
        {
          "id": "doc-67fcc48de84f::sentence-293",
          "documentId": "doc-67fcc48de84f",
          "text": "McSally | McSally | Republican | AZ | Yea |\n",
          "start": 13070,
          "end": 13114,
          "context": "McNerney | McNerney | Democratic | CA | Nay |\n McSally | McSally | Republican | AZ | Yea |\n Meadows | Meadows | Republican | NC | Yea |\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-b7039c2b13f6::sentence-7",
          "documentId": "doc-b7039c2b13f6",
          "text": "I support reform such as modernizing the retirement age and indexing it to life expectancy. ",
          "start": 654,
          "end": 746,
          "context": "But no longer can we simply “protect” Social Security as some politicians seek to do; we must make needed reforms to “preserve” it for future generations.  I support reform such as modernizing the retirement age and indexing it to life expectancy.  I also support giving younger workers the opportunity to invest a portion of their money in optional personal accounts. "
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-b7039c2b13f6::sentence-5",
          "documentId": "doc-b7039c2b13f6",
          "text": "SITTON: Our nation must keep our commitment to seniors and people nearing retirement to assure they get the benefits they have planned on. ",
          "start": 360,
          "end": 499,
          "context": "Answers:\n SITTON: Our nation must keep our commitment to seniors and people nearing retirement to assure they get the benefits they have planned on.  But no longer can we simply “protect” Social Security as some politicians seek to do; we must make needed reforms to “preserve” it for future generations. "
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-b7039c2b13f6::sentence-2",
          "documentId": "doc-b7039c2b13f6",
          "text": "Is Social Security, as it now exists, survivable and would you support raising the cap on earning, raising the retirement age, reducing payments to wealthier Americans and allow younger workers to invest a portion of the Social Security into private accounts? ",
          "start": 11,
          "end": 271,
          "context": "Question 3\n Is Social Security, as it now exists, survivable and would you support raising the cap on earning, raising the retirement age, reducing payments to wealthier Americans and allow younger workers to invest a portion of the Social Security into private accounts?  What proposals would you make to ensure it is available for future generations?\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-67fcc48de84f::sentence-229",
          "documentId": "doc-67fcc48de84f",
