        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "atomId": "atom-3",
      "spans": [
        {
          "id": "doc-b7039c2b13f6::sentence-7",
          "documentId": "doc-b7039c2b13f6",
          "text": "I support reform such as modernizing the retirement age and indexing it to life expectancy. ",
          "start": 654,
          "end": 746,
          "context": "But no longer can we simply “protect” Social Security as some politicians seek to do; we must make needed reforms to “preserve” it for future generations.  I support reform such as modernizing the retirement age and indexing it to life expectancy.  I also support giving younger workers the opportunity to invest a portion of their money in optional personal accounts. "
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-67fcc48de84f::sentence-293",
          "documentId": "doc-67fcc48de84f",
          "text": "McSally | McSally | Republican | AZ | Yea |\n",
          "start": 13070,
          "end": 13114,
          "context": "McNerney | McNerney | Democratic | CA | Nay |\n McSally | McSally | Republican | AZ | Yea |\n Meadows | Meadows | Republican | NC | Yea |\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-b7039c2b13f6::sentence-2",
          "documentId": "doc-b7039c2b13f6",
          "text": "Is Social Security, as it now exists, survivable and would you support raising the cap on earning, raising the retirement age, reducing payments to wealthier Americans and allow younger workers to invest a portion of the Social Security into private accounts? ",
          "start": 11,
          "end": 271,
          "context": "Question 3\n Is Social Security, as it now exists, survivable and would you support raising the cap on earning, raising the retirement age, reducing payments to wealthier Americans and allow younger workers to invest a portion of the Social Security into private accounts?  What proposals would you make to ensure it is available for future generations?\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-b7039c2b13f6::sentence-14",
          "documentId": "doc-b7039c2b13f6",
          "text": "For younger workers, we need to consider approaches such as gradually increasing the retirement age and allowing them to invest a portion of their Social Security payments in ways that will allow them to maximize their returns. ",
          "start": 1410,
          "end": 1638,
          "context": "At the same time, we have take measures to strengthen and sustain it for future generations because it is currently unsustainable.  For younger workers, we need to consider approaches such as gradually increasing the retirement age and allowing them to invest a portion of their Social Security payments in ways that will allow them to maximize their returns.  We also need to stop raiding the retirement fund at will for special interests so we can keep our promises and institute the measures needed to strengthen and sustain social security for future generations.\n"
        },
        {
          "id": "doc-67fcc48de84f::sentence-274",
          "documentId": "doc-67fcc48de84f",
          "text": "MacArthur | MacArthur | Republican | NJ | Yea |\n",
